What is the Java code to analyze the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on global stock markets and its potential long-term effects on the world economy? Can you also provide insights on how the pandemic contributed to the shift towards remote work and digital technologies? Please include relevant Java code to support your analysis.
To analyze the impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on global stock markets, you can use the following Java code:
import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Scanner;
public class StockMarketAnalysis {
  public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
    File file = new File("stock_market_data.csv");
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(file);
    double total_loss = 0;
    int num_losses = 0;
    while (sc.hasNextLine()) {
      String[] line = sc.nextLine().split(",");
      double change = Double.parseDouble(line[1]);
      if (change < 0) {
        total_loss += change;
        num_losses++;
      }
    }
    System.out.println("Total loss in stock market: " + total_loss);
    System.out.println("Average loss per day: " + (total_loss / num_losses));
  }
}
To analyze the potential long-term effects on the world economy, you can use the following Java code:
import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Scanner;
public class WorldEconomyAnalysis {
  public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
    File file = new File("world_economy_data.csv");
    Scanner sc = new Scanner(file);
    double gdp_growth = 0;
    int num_years = 0;
    while (sc.hasNextLine()) {
      String[] line = sc.nextLine().split(",");
      double growth = Double.parseDouble(line[1]);
      gdp_growth += growth;
      num_years++;
    }
    System.out.println("Total GDP growth since the pandemic: " + gdp_growth);
    System.out.println("Average GDP growth per year: " + (gdp_growth / num_years));
  }
}
