To analyze Helena's character in "A Midsummer Night's Dream" using Latex data format, we can use Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques in Python. We can start by extracting the text from the play and then using NLP libraries like spaCy and NLTK to tokenize, parse, and analyze the text.
Here's an example code snippet to extract the text of the play:
```python
import requests
url = 'https://www.gutenberg.org/files/1514/1514-0.txt'
response = requests.get(url)
text = response.text
# Extract the text of the play
start = text.find('ACT I')
end = text.find('FINIS')
play_text = text[start:end]
```
Next, we can use spaCy to tokenize and parse the text:
```python
import spacy
nlp = spacy.load('en_core_web_sm')
doc = nlp(play_text)
# Print the tokens
for token in doc:
    print(token.text, token.pos_, token.dep_)
```
