    // Print analysis results
    fmt.Printf("Comparing %s to %s:\n", iPhone12.name, iPhone11.name)
    fmt.Printf("- Battery life improved by %.2f%%\n", batteryLifeImprovement)
    fmt.Printf("- Processor speed improved by %.2f%%\n", processorSpeedImprovement)
    // Discuss implications for app performance
    if batteryLifeImprovement > 0 {
        fmt.Println("\nGiven the improved battery life, users may be able to use apps for longer periods of time without needing to recharge their iPhone.")
    } else {
        fmt.Println("\nGiven the comparable battery life, users may not experience significant differences in app usage.")
    }
    if processorSpeedImprovement > 0 {
        fmt.Println("\nGiven the improved processor speed, apps may run faster and smoother on the iPhone 12 compared to the iPhone 11.")
    } else {
        fmt.Println("\nGiven the comparable processor speed, users may not experience significant differences in app performance.")
    }
}
```
This code defines a `struct` called `iPhoneModel` that contains the name of the iPhone model, its battery life in hours, and its processor speed in GHz. It then creates two instances of this struct for the iPhone 11 and iPhone 12 models, and calculates the percentage improvements in battery life and processor speed between the two models.
The code then prints out the analysis results, and uses conditional statements to discuss the potential implications for app performance based on the battery life and processor speed improvements.
Note that this code only considers two quantitative factors (battery life and processor speed) and their impact on app performance. To incorporate qualitative factors, you could add additional fields to the `iPhoneModel` struct (such as user reviews or ratings), and modify the analysis and discussion accordingly.

